This is a placeholder, not an entitlement certificate. It is a throwaway
self-signed certificate that authenticates nothing. It exists so that this
example fragment mount subtree derives the same mount points as a live
entitlement fragment, and so that the two are interchangeable by a one-line
change to the image reference in a manifest.

Build your own fragment from your own entitlement material and publish it to
a registry you control. See docs/fragment-format.md.

Keep the text above free of the colon character. A colon inside or above a PEM
block crashes the certificate parser in python3-subscription-manager-rhsm
1.30.12 with SIGSEGV, which turns a diagnosable build failure into a bare
segmentation fault.

